  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, which passes the typecheck. I haven't run it in a browser or built it, so the rendering is unchecked. The scene is a low-poly island with animated water and a 20-second day/night cycle.\n\n- **Island:** the terrain is a flat-shaded mesh with one normal and one colour per face. The colours run sand, grass, rock and snow by height. About 46 trees (cone crowns on cylinder trunks) and 16 low-segment sphere rocks sit on it, placed from the same height function.\n- **Water:** a 150 m wave-displaced mesh with a custom shader. It has faceted normals, a fresnel blend towards the sky colour, sun or moon glints, and light crest highlights. It is slightly transparent, so the sand shows through at the shore.\n- **Day/night:** each frame moves the sun and moon lights, the Preetham sky (with stars), the ambient light and the fog colour. The water shader's colours and light direction follow too. At night the sun is off, and the moon plus the ambient light keep the scene lit.\n- **Camera:** it sits 20 m above the water and orbits slowly around the island at 42 m.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`.\n\nI couldn't confirm that the transparent custom water blends as intended or how the framing looks.\n\n",
